@startuml Convoy Operations Use Cases

title Use cases: planning and running a convoy
caption Target design. Convoy operations. Decisions D17, P14, O36, O27, O20, O2, O8, O24, O25, X7. ADRs 0007, 0008, 0009, 0010, 0015, 0016.

left to right direction

actor Purchaser as purch
actor Mechanic as mech
actor Dispatcher as disp
actor Administrator as admin
actor "Convoy Leader\n(own convoy only)" as leader
actor "Other drivers" as drivers

rectangle "Freedom" {
  usecase "Source a vehicle" as V1
  usecase "Record a vehicle inspection" as V2
  usecase "Create a convoy and its route" as C1
  usecase "Build and publish the truck list" as C2
  usecase "Set budget and vehicle equipment" as C3
  usecase "Seat crew" as C4
  usecase "Nominate or reassign\nthe Convoy Leader" as C5
  usecase "Record insurance" as C6
  usecase "Book ferries and accommodation" as C7
  usecase "Set handover Receivers" as C8
  usecase "Allocate boxes to vehicles" as C9
  usecase "Sign off a vehicle's load" as C10
  usecase "Review readiness" as C11
  usecase "Depart the convoy" as C12
  usecase "Mark route points and crossings" as R1
  usecase "Enter fuel" as R2
  usecase "Record box outcomes" as R3
  usecase "Record goods-list acceptance" as R4
  usecase "Read route and Receiver addresses" as R5
  usecase "Mark the convoy arrived" as E1
  usecase "Close the convoy and read the report" as E2
}

purch --> V1
mech --> V2
admin --> V2
disp --> C1
disp --> C2
disp --> C3
disp --> C4
disp --> C5
admin --> C5
disp --> C6
disp --> C7
disp --> C8
disp --> C9
admin --> C10
disp --> C11
disp --> C12
leader --> R1
disp --> R1
leader --> R2
leader --> R3
disp --> R3
leader --> R4
disp --> R4
leader --> R5
disp --> E1
disp --> E2

leader ..> drivers : radio
C12 ..> C11 : <<include>>

note right of R1
  A Dispatcher records marks on the
  leader's behalf, named (O27).
end note

note right of R5
  From 14 days before departure until
  arrival or reassignment; audited.
  Other drivers are given no addresses (O1).
end note

note right of C12
  Refused until every blocking
  requirement holds; no override (O3).
end note

@enduml
